# Count-Up Animations

Any numeric value in a scorecard — and anything that visibly moves from 0 to a
number — must animate a count-up.

## Rules for the agent

- Every scorecard number animates a count-up on load.
- Where charts are re-animatable (see `pages/analytics-types.html`), clicking a
  chart must re-run its animation, including the count-up.
- Reuse the shared count-up implementation (`js/count-up-all.js` /
  `js/count-up.js`). Do not add ad-hoc one-off counters.
- Large "hero" numbers (e.g. the food count on wiseai.html) should ramp quickly
  and settle, not crawl.

## Verify

When testing, allow real wall-clock time for count-ups to settle before
screenshotting (see the `visual-verify` skill).
